  "steps": "The steps of `node scripts/identity-proof.mjs demo wss://nos.lol wss://nostr.mom`: two disposable keys are made, the BCH key and the Nostr key are linked in one signed binding event (kind 7428), the event is published to both relays, read back from each relay separately and verified from the relay data alone, and then both keys answer a challenge from a separate relying application.",
  "how": "Run in a Chromium browser on the owner's computer (the cloud workspace used for this work cannot open WebSockets to public relays). The browser loaded this repository's own modules (packages/decentralized-identity/index.mjs, packages/chain-observer/primitives.mjs, config/network.mjs) from GitHub at commit 033129902fd13ba94034e40026d39419abfbf2d3 through jsDelivr, with @noble/curves 2.0.1, @noble/hashes 2.0.1, @bitauth/libauth 3.0.0 and buffer 6.0.3 from esm.sh (the versions in package-lock.json). The code that strings the steps together is the demo branch of scripts/identity-proof.mjs, with crypto.getRandomValues in place of node:crypto.",
  "network": "chipnet (the default of scripts/identity-proof.mjs; the address in the binding is a test-network address). No BCH transaction, no account and no game data are involved.",
